        "original_id": "47d91e1f-dcfa-54ac-b103-11abbc6be1ae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Sítio do Picapau Amarelo, The Chronicles of Narnia, O Saci\n- People: C. S. Lewis, L. Frank Baum\n- Topics: Brazilian children's literature, family films, literary adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- The Chronicles of Narnia is a series of seven fantasy novels by C. S. Lewis.\n- Sítio do Picapau Amarelo is considered representative of Brazilian children's literature.\n- Sítio do Picapau Amarelo is described as the Brazilian equivalent of children's classics such as C. S. Lewis's The Chronicles of Narnia and L. Frank Baum's The Wonderful Wizard of Oz series.\n- O Saci is noted as the first family film made in Brazil.\n- O Saci is the first theatrical adaptation of Sítio do Picapau Amarelo.",
